---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="resume -- alexander campos" description="Alexander Campos - six years in regulated bank operations: vendor integrations, controls, SOP governance, and the tooling behind them.">
  <article class="resume">
    <header class="masthead">
      <h1>Alexander Campos</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Banking operations · programs, controls &amp; automation</p>
      <p class="contact-line">
        Washington D.C. Metro Area <span aria-hidden="true">|</span>
        <a href="mailto:alex@campos.works">alex@campos.works</a> <span aria-hidden="true">|</span>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/alexander-d-campos">linkedin.com/in/alexander-d-campos</a> <span aria-hidden="true">|</span>
        <a href="https://campos.works">campos.works</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <ul class="stats" aria-label="At a glance">
      <li><b>6 yrs</b><span>regulated finance ops</span></li>
      <li><b>~80</b><span>people, SOP governance managed</span></li>
      <li><b>$600M+</b><span>regulatory network monitored</span></li>
      <li><b>78%</b><span>less manual review</span></li>
      <li><b>20,000+</b><span>account failure resolved solo</span></li>
      <li><b>38+</b><span>vendor integrations owned</span></li>
      <li><b>50+ hrs</b><span>cut in one quarter</span></li>
    </ul>

    <section class="summary">
      <p>
        Six years in regulated bank operations, starting on a teller line and promoted
        four times in five years. Built the monitoring behind a $600M+ regulatory network
        (78% less manual review), resolved a 20,000-account logic failure independently,
        and onboarded a merger's law firm vendors with zero transmission errors. Works on
        one principle: do the work well or not at all, and spend human judgment, which is
        finite, on the problems that return the most.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Experience</h2>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div class="role-top">
            <h3 class="org">Capital One</h3>
            <span class="dates">Richmond, VA · June 2025 – Present</span>
          </div>
          <p class="title">Senior Process Manager, Card Legal Recoveries Operations</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Vendor integrations:</strong> own the technical integration framework and Systems Integration Guide for 38+ national vendors, a repeatable onboarding method spanning technical specifications, file ingestion, testing cycles, production readiness, and go-live.</li>
          <li><strong>Discover merger integration:</strong> owned the Systems Integration Guide for onboarding the legacy third-party law firm vendors; delivered zero transmission errors in that scope, catching specification failures before production cutover.</li>
          <li><strong>Roadmap:</strong> defined a 5-month modernization roadmap with dependency sequencing, approval gates, and rollback protocols.</li>
          <li><strong>Controls and monitoring:</strong> run controls and observability for a $600M+ regulated file-exchange network with 300+ daily transmissions. Took anomaly detection from a rapid prototype to an automated pipeline, cutting manual monitoring 78% and shipping two formally owned production controls.</li>
          <li><strong>Root-cause analysis:</strong> resolved a 20,000+ account logic failure independently: built the SQL investigation, isolated root cause, remediated, and stood up monitoring on what it exposed.</li>
          <li><strong>Reporting and analysis:</strong> built an automated business-review pipeline spanning six teams and 20+ operational data points; leaders three levels up use its one-pagers for quarterly reviews. The department's go-to for ad-hoc data questions, from account ledgers to QA metrics.</li>
          <li><strong>Executive briefing:</strong> briefed newly inherited senior leadership during the merger transition on the end-to-end third-party monitoring architecture and its supplier risk; the briefing was elevated to the next executive level and recognized for audience tailoring and delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>AI in remediation:</strong> became the team's go-to resource for using AI tools in remediation workflows; built a repeatable method with validated instruction sets and human judgment on every decision, and wrote the guides other teams picked up.</li>
          <li><strong>SOP governance:</strong> manage the SOP library, annual audits, and ownership mapping for a department of ~80 people across 8-9 teams.</li>
          <li><strong>Beyond the role:</strong> floating technical lead at a 140-associate enterprise AI summit, coaching teams through problem decomposition; volunteer Gemini instructor at an enterprise event; mentor to management development associates.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div class="role-top">
            <h3 class="org">Apple Federal Credit Union</h3>
            <span class="dates">Fairfax &amp; Lake Ridge, VA · January 2020 – May 2025</span>
          </div>
          <p class="title">Branch Operations Administrator</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Promoted four times in five years:</strong> Teller, Member Advisor (consumer lending), Assistant Branch Manager, Branch Operations Administrator. Completed bachelor's degree concurrently.</li>
          <li><strong>Assistant Branch Manager</strong> (July 2021 – December 2023): ran daily operations for a high-volume branch, leading a team of seven; owned escalations, branch audits, and staff coaching.</li>
          <li><strong>Enterprise support:</strong> service and operations support across 25 branches through a major merger; contributed to all-time high NPS and the lowest audit findings per branch in over a decade.</li>
          <li><strong>Modernization and reporting:</strong> built a branch-wide modernization plan and presented it to the CEO with VP and SVP backing (approved and implemented); built compliance reporting in Power BI and cut complaint response cycles 50%.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <div class="role-top">
            <h3 class="org">AI evaluation &amp; projects</h3>
            <span class="dates">2025 – Present</span>
          </div>
          <p class="title">Contract and personal work</p>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Model evaluation (contract, 2026):</strong> authored adversarial evaluation tasks for OpenAI's GDPVal benchmark in finance through LinkedIn's AI Trainer program: scenario design, weighted pass/fail rubrics, and golden answers. Consultant on a legal hold and discovery evaluation batch.</li>
          <li><strong>Tooling and personal projects:</strong> built a small workbench for authoring benchmark tasks; also a <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@forgeframe/server">memory server for AI agents</a> (MIT licensed, on npm) and <a href="https://reframed.works">Reframed</a>, a live web application built and run solo (Next.js, TypeScript, Postgres).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Skills</h2>

      <h3>Program &amp; Operations</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        Program delivery · Vendor and third-party integrations · Dependency sequencing ·
        Test and go-live readiness · Controls design · Root-cause analysis · Executive reporting
      </p>

      <h3>Technical</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        SQL (Postgres, Snowflake) · Python · TypeScript · Splunk · Observe · Power BI ·
        Tableau · APIs and data pipelines
      </p>

      <h3>AI</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        Applied AI in operations workflows · Model evaluation and rubric design ·
        Agent workflows · Local open-weight models
      </p>

      <h3>Languages</h3>
      <p class="skills">English and Spanish (native bilingual)</p>

      <h3>Regulated Finance</h3>
      <p class="skills">
        Third-party risk · Change control · BSA/AML/KYC · SCRA · TILA/Reg Z ·
        FDCPA/Reg F · NCUA · CFPB
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Education &amp; certifications</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>B.S. Business Administration, Management and Operations</strong> -- George Mason
        University, December 2024.
      </p>
      <p class="skills">
        AI Governance Professional (AIGP, IAPP) -- expected December 2026 ·
        Business Process Management (2024) · Google Data Analytics (2024)
      </p>
    </section>

  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    console.log(
      '%c same question, different shapes. ',
      'color: #5BF29B; font-family: monospace; font-size: 11px;'
    );
  </script>
</Page>

<style>
  .resume {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .skills {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--white-60);
  }

  .role {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .role-header {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .role-header h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }

  .dates {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--white-45);
  }

  .role ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .role li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .role li strong {
    color: var(--glow-hot);
  }

  .resume-contact {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .resume-contact p {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--white-45);
  }
  .stats {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--white-15); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-15);
  }
  .stats li {
    padding: 0.85rem 0.5rem; text-align: center;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--white-08);
  }
  .stats li:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .stats b {
    font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1;
    color: var(--glow-hot); letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .stats span {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--white-45); line-height: 1.35;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } .stats li:nth-child(4) { border-right: none; } }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .stats li { border-right: none; } }

  /* ── The PDF's grammar, carried over ──
     Centered masthead, gold small-caps section rules, company in gold with
     place and dates on the right, italic title, tight bullets with bold leads.
     The stat strip is the one thing the paper version does not have. */
  .resume { font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .masthead { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .masthead h1 { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.04em; margin: 0 0 0.3rem; }
  .subtitle { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold-accent); margin: 0 0 0.55rem; }
  .contact-line { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--white-45); margin: 0; }
  .contact-line a { color: var(--white-60); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-15); }
  .contact-line a:hover { color: var(--gold-accent); border-bottom-color: var(--gold-accent); }
  .contact-line span { color: var(--white-15); margin: 0 0.4rem; }

  .resume .summary p { color: var(--white-70); max-width: 72ch; margin: 0; }
  .resume hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--white-08); margin: 1.6rem 0; }

  .resume h2 {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-accent); font-weight: 500; margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold-accent); opacity: 0.95;
  }
  .resume .role { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .resume .role-header { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  .role-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .resume .org { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.12rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--gold-accent); margin: 0; }
  .resume .dates { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--white-45); white-space: nowrap; }
  .resume .title { font-style: italic; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--white-60); margin: 0.1rem 0 0; }
  .resume .role ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .resume .role li { margin: 0 0 0.45rem; color: var(--white-70); }
  .resume .role li strong { color: var(--glow-hot); font-weight: 600; }
  .resume .role li a { color: var(--glow-hot); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--white-15); text-decoration: none; }

  .resume h3:not(.org) { font-family: var(--body); font-size: 0.86rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--glow-hot); margin: 0.7rem 0 0.2rem; }
  .resume .skills { font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .masthead h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
    .resume .dates { white-space: normal; }
    .contact-line span { display: none; }
    .contact-line a { display: block; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  }
</style>
